        "category": "classfeature",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>The staff is perhaps the simplest of weapons, but this simplicity belies its elegance and versatility. To you, a staff is casting implement and martial weapon alike—the foundation of a fighting style.</p>\n<p>While you wield a staff in one hand, the staff adjusts in shape and weight, gaining the agile trait and increasing its damage die size to 1d6. While you wield a staff in both hands, it lengthens, twists, and reshapes, gaining the parry, reach, and trip traits.</p>\n<p>While you're in @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Arcane Cascade] stance, once per round you can Interact to change your grip on a staff as a free action.</p>\n<p><strong>Conflux Spell</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Spinning Staff]</p>\n<p><strong>Studious Spells</strong> 7th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Oaken Resilience]; 11th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Slow]; 13th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Flicker]</p>"
